1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
TENGER: see the sky change in NASA SPHEREx images.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Real images, 2010 and 2026: Barnard's Star moved.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:13,000
We locked a Pluto forecast in GitHub
before opening the newest images.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
6 arcsec off: 3,000x closer than a straight line,
but just outside our 95% region. A published miss.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
We found why, and froze new forecasts for 2027.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Could SPHEREx see Planet X? We measured it: for the nominal
Planet Nine, one image is 4 to 7 magnitudes too shallow.
